    "knowledge_point": "Integrating Products Containing the Exponential Function",
    "problem": "$\\int 8{x}^{3}{e}^{4-{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
    "worked_solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=4-{x}^{4}.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4{x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,-2\\text{d}u=8{x}^{3}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8{x}^{3}{e}^{4-{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{4-{x}^{4}}\\cdot 8{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{u}\\cdot (-2)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2{e}^{u}+C \\\\  & =-2{e}^{4-{x}^{4}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
